findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote config loading tests but none specifically test that parse errors
    or permission failures are distinguished from NotFound. Dev implemented from_file_or_default
    using unwrap_or_default pattern. Reviewer did not flag this specific issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Reviewer verified: ''ServerError Display says "server error: request
    failed" regardless of the inner string. The inner String is only accessible via
    Debug, not Display.'' TEA also wrote CWE-209 tests in exit_codes.rs. However,
    the CliError Display for Io(#[error(transparent)]) still forwards full OS error
    details to stderr, which was not flagged.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CRLF header injection tests for tenant ID. Dev implemented\
    \ CRLF checking. However, the finding is about using raw String instead of TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core \u2014 the type-safety aspect was NOT caught. Only the injection\
    \ symptom was partially mitigated via runtime checks, not the root cause (wrong\
    \ type)."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. TEA added workspace dependencies but the crate Cargo.toml
    apparently uses direct versions for some deps.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields\
    \ \u2014 no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]' and specifically noted 'A TOML file\
    \ with sevrer_timeout = 30 (typo) silently ignores the mistyped key.' This covers\
    \ the token field scenario."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw
    was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote tests but did not flag this pattern in existing
    or generated tests.
